[{"id":3108065719,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc65QVG3","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50084500?u=188e88b24d6994108226c9c94ad225775258d6ef&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Geometror","id":50084500,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMDg0NTAw","login":"Geometror","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geometror"},"body":"Tested locally and it seems to work :)\r\nCode looks good.\r\n(While this technically does break compat with modules I don't think this is a problem here)","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109517#pullrequestreview-3108065719","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109517","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-08-11T23:35:18Z"},{"id":3109279563,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc65U9dL","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"I'm not sure if this is the best fix for the issue.\r\nIt seems like `get_persistent_signal_connection_count` is used to determine if a signal was actually disconnected.\r\n\r\nA different solution might be to return a boolean from `Object::disconnect` which informs whether a disconnect happened. It seems like `Object::disconnect` is calling `_disconnect`, which _does_ return a bool. While it is not documented what the bool does, it seems like it might fit the bill.\r\nIf `disconnect` was made to return that bool, and further uresd for the update check instead of calling `get_persistent_signal_connection_count`, it may be possible to eliminate unnecessary lookups, reducing the lookup speed further without introducing new optimization logic.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109517#pullrequestreview-3109279563","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109517","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-08-12T08:39:05Z"},{"id":3114392344,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc65odsY","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Looks good to me! Thank you for being open to change the approach :)","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109517#pullrequestreview-3114392344","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109517","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-08-13T08:00:04Z"},{"id":3114416315,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc65oji7","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"u